#: ../../source/docs/stall-prevention.rst:91
#: 6904d99a4c4d471282f3e1e199e10c5e
msgid "Example Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stall-prevention.rst:93
#: 63206dd5348d414193b127b04ef6cd27
msgid "An example of how stall prevention works is in AUTO mode when making a turn for an automated landing. The landing approach will aim for an airspeed of :ref:`TECS_LAND_ARSPD <TECS_LAND_ARSPD>`, which is often quite low, and may be just above the stall speed. If the final turn is sharp (it is often 90 degrees) the plane may be trying to perform a sharp turn while dropping speed for landing. That could induce a stall. The stall prevention code means two things happen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stall-prevention.rst:101
#: a5db208bb8b64d55870d43ddbfff8f87
msgid "the initial turn is kept shallow enough to prevent the stall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stall-prevention.rst:102
#: 8163302b772b434cad933011ab9ff5c2
msgid "the target airspeed is kept high enough during the turn to allow the turn to complete, after which it is lowered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stall-prevention.rst:106
#: 0bc63f213b2a473899ddd3a9f3f549d8
msgid "Nose Down in FBWA and AUTOTUNE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stall-prevention.rst:108
#: cccd21f35d9b43b381394cfda848e5b3
msgid "The FBWA mode has an additional special feature to help prevent straight line stalls. It is often difficult for a pilot to judge the airspeed of a plane when it is coming head on, and so many pilots find themselves flying too slow when they are trying to fly gently in FBWA mode. This is especially true if the ArduPilot pitch controller is well tuned and manages to keep the nose up even when flying slowly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stall-prevention.rst:115
#: bedc2570560842bba87fb986dab58385
msgid "To make a level flight low speed stall less likely some additional down pitch is added in FBWA and AUTOTUNE modes based on the throttle position. The amount of down pitch added is based on the :ref:`STAB_PITCH_DOWN <STAB_PITCH_DOWN>` parameter, which defaults to 2 degrees. At zero throttle this full down pitch is added. If throttle is above ``TRIM_THROTTLE`` then no down pitch is added. Between those two values the down pitch is added in proportion to the throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stall-prevention.rst:124
#: ed375187695040d4a1e9909330cbc933
msgid "This has the effect of slightly lowering the nose when you lower throttle in FBWA and AUTOTUNE modes, which makes the plane gain a bit of speed, and thus makes it less likely to stall. The value you need for ``STAB_PITCH_DOWN`` depends on how much drag your plane has. A very sleek model will need a smaller value. A high drag model will need a larger value."
msgstr ""
